.TH BEEMR 1 2026-10-03 "beemr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
beemr \- peer\-to\-peer file sharing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B beemr share
.I path
.RB [ \-\-to
.IR device ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR count ]
.RB [ \-e
.IR time ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-port\-mapping ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-relay ]
.RB [ \-\-copy ]
.br
.B beemr get
.I ticket
.RB [ \-o
.IR folder ]
.br
.B beemr
.RB { setup | id | name | contact | relay | doctor | help | version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B beemr
sends files and folders straight to another device, with no servers,
accounts or setup.
It connects directly when it can (same network, IPv6, or a port opened on the
router with UPnP, PCP or NAT\-PMP), punches through NATs when it can't (hole
punching, or port prediction for strict NATs), and otherwise relays through
another beemr device or, as a last resort, Tor.
Both sides print a
.B How:
line naming the path a transfer took.
Devices find each other through signed records on the BitTorrent Mainline DHT.
All traffic is end\-to\-end encrypted.
.PP
Every device has a cryptographic identity, created on first use, and a name
chosen by its user.
Names of devices that are not saved as contacts are shown as unverified.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "share " path
Share a file or folder and print a
.B beemr get
command for the other device.
By default the share allows one download and never expires.
.TP
.BI "get " ticket
Download a share into the current folder, or the folder given with
.BR \-o .
Files are saved under a free name and are never overwritten.
.TP
.B setup
Name this device.
.TP
.B id
Print this device's ID, which others use to reach it.
.TP
.BR name " [" \fInew\ name\fR ]
Show or change this device's name.
.TP
.BR contact " {" add " \fIname id\fR | " list " | " remove " \fIname\fR}"
Manage saved contacts.
.TP
.BR relay " {" run " [" \-\-private "] [" \-\-port " \fIport\fR] | " use " \fIaddress\fR | " list " | " remove " \fIaddress\fR}"
Run a relay for devices that can't connect directly, or configure relays to use.
.TP
.B doctor
Report how reachable this device is: local network, IPv6, router port
mapping, network (NAT) type, direct reachability, hole punching and relays.
.SH SHARE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-to " contact\-or\-id"
Only this device may download.
Repeat for several devices.
.TP
.BI "\-n, \-\-downloads " count
Number of downloads to allow (default 1; 0 means unlimited).
.TP
.BI "\-e, \-\-expires " time
Stop accepting downloads after a time such as 30s, 10m, 2h or 1d.
.TP
.BI "\-p, \-\-port " port
Listen on this TCP and UDP port instead of a random one.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-port\-mapping
Don't ask the router to open a port with UPnP, PCP or NAT\-PMP.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-relay
Don't relay end\-to\-end encrypted traffic for other beemr users while
sharing.
By default, a sharer that is reachable from the internet relays for devices
that can't connect directly, until the share ends.
.TP
.B \-\-copy
Copy the
.B beemr get
command to the system clipboard.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BEEMR_HOME
Folder for the identity and contacts (default
.I ~/.config/beemr
on Linux).
.TP
.B BEEMR_LOG
Diagnostic logging, for example
.BR BEEMR_LOG=debug .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/beemr/identity
This device's private key.
.TP
.I ~/.config/beemr/contacts
Saved contacts.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
beemr share photos/ \-n 3 \-e 2h
beemr share contract.pdf \-\-to sara
beemr get <ticket> \-o ~/Downloads
beemr contact add Sara <device\-id>
beemr share report.pdf \-\-to sara
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/osmanahmadxai/beemr
